#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059672 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059500 :question/id #uuid "35535b08-b3d8-5037-a821-6815577169d2" :question/math-academy-id "e-3618" :question/problem "Without using a calculator, find the exact value of $$\n\\displaystyle \\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\sin{x}\\cos{x} = \\sin{2x}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(2\\cdot \\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right) .\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{24}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{24}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\left[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{24}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{24}\\right)\\right]\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\dfrac{\\pi}{12},$ we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\left[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\right] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\left[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{12}\\right)\\right] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\sin{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{24}\\right)}\\cos{\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}\\right)} = \\dfrac{1}{8}.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d820aa9f-7c02-53b5-9b09-c25ee59dbdaf" :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186749695 :question-generator/id #uuid "50a21fc9-aa2a-5273-9421-9d7d97a4704e" :question-generator/script "generators/93/9337de33429f720e400d28159cee11e07a426ad39530af33b9646bd7c5af67bf/generator.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060239 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f5e037a-d907-5e75-8572-a21f2f100b86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288697} {:answer/id #uuid "6b4c0f05-ccdb-59d1-bb07-0330ee61384f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288788} {:answer/id #uuid "add73e65-c6fc-54b3-86a9-efe0ea9d1061" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1+\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289183} {:answer/id #uuid "bfeaf92c-dcea-5028-acba-166e92cd2d93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289300} {:answer/id #uuid "fc31e4ba-f99c-51b0-b6f7-de76a067ff38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f5e037a-d907-5e75-8572-a21f2f100b86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288697} :answer-field/id #uuid "b85596f7-12df-574c-9e94-581ddb2bf096" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290132}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b22f045c-0b9c-53f1-b536-66fda02ca447" :question/math-academy-id "q-24361" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={7.5}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {7.5}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({15}^{∘}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) & =2\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({15}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x={15}^{∘},$ we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{15}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{15}^{∘}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {15}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({30}^{∘})\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({7.5}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({15}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡({30}^{∘})=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060243 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93710ca5-6027-591d-969f-097bebd99547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\sin \\left(\\frac{π}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058101} {:answer/id #uuid "dafb79ee-0595-52df-b01e-9c1753d35db9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\sin \\left(\\frac{π}{6}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058102} {:answer/id #uuid "e1131cf8-b01f-5702-9ca2-a730156984f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\sin \\left(\\frac{π}{6}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058103} {:answer/id #uuid "3af60303-8273-5e10-9f8e-89a0cc111a4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sin \\left(\\frac{π}{6}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058104} {:answer/id #uuid "7b156a1e-b747-5820-8472-2b68ebe1b1db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin \\left(\\frac{π}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058105}] :answer-field/id #uuid "df1354db-d1d7-54db-baba-68ca0802536b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058100}] :question/id #uuid "0ab58d1b-4097-516b-91bf-48c130e66ed2" :question/math-academy-id "q-24648" :question/problem "What is $$\n\\displaystyle 6\\sin \\left(\\frac{π}{12}\\right)\\cos \\left(\\frac{π}{12}\\right)\\cos \\left(\\frac{π}{6}\\right)\n$$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233282 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18c9b4b1-1095-5f9b-afce-633347485f56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}\\operatorname{csc}⁡({75}^{∘})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250770} {:answer/id #uuid "299c5f87-5d49-5061-92a3-1c662ad07f92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250909} {:answer/id #uuid "70aa70e8-91d7-536f-ae22-f835158dcb12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{csc}⁡({75}^{∘})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251473} {:answer/id #uuid "aeec17ba-9e38-5bb4-bd85-072a01d4cd00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252077} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb91b61-0767-56e9-b516-9be479319ff9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{sin}⁡({150}^{∘})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252645}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aeec17ba-9e38-5bb4-bd85-072a01d4cd00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252077} :answer-field/id #uuid "6946fb4a-fa21-51f2-b279-830394eb4469" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252998}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8883bfa3-8f36-5e8a-8a63-990442c2b246" :question/math-academy-id "q-120087" :question/problem "$10\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}⁡({150}^{∘})=$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={75}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {75}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({150}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}⁡({150}^{∘}) & =5\\cdot [2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘})]\\operatorname{csc}⁡({150}^{∘}) \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{sin}⁡({150}^{∘})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({150}^{∘})} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233283 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "19bb82ee-2583-57ae-92ec-48971505d385" :question/math-academy-id "q-120094" :question/problem "Find the exact value of $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{\\operatorname{sec}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)}{\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}x\\operatorname{cos}x=\\operatorname{sin}2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{16}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)=\\operatorname{sin}\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)=\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right).\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sec}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)}{\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sec}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)}{2\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sec}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)}{\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\frac{\\pi }{8}$, we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)} & =\\frac{4}{2\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{sin}\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{sin}\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\right)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253642 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c52498f