me{csc}⁡({140}^{∘}) & =2\\cdot [2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘})]\\operatorname{csc}⁡({140}^{∘}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253643 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04698c75-dc83-5fbb-8f53-9052909b1e30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250585} {:answer/id #uuid "1b2c3035-0235-5603-a72a-eb385d8843e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250786} {:answer/id #uuid "6012bda1-9035-5aff-82de-2b534c046c57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251340} {:answer/id #uuid "9aad87db-038e-549a-b557-3d3499e0f30c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251882} {:answer/id #uuid "df46eab3-2fa6-5ef3-9539-002572011a52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6012bda1-9035-5aff-82de-2b534c046c57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251340} :answer-field/id #uuid "e90d146b-981f-56ed-88e6-d9ffffc3ab01" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253212}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "91b3ae38-a411-55e5-ba0c-b0976c1d82dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-120093" :question/problem "$$\n\\displaystyle 8\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)=\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{32}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right).\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right) & =4\\left[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{32}\\right)\\right]\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\frac{\\pi }{16},$ we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right) & =2\\left[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)\\right] \\\\  & =2\\left[\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{16}\\right)\\right] \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290559 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "250cdf52-80dd-5fc2-af4b-70ef347a1cea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/ma